	A demon is summoned
      </p>
    </abilitydescription>
  </ability>


  <ability>
    <abilitytitle>Swarm</abilitytitle>
    <abilityid>swarm</abilityid>
    <abilityranks from="1" to="1"/>
    <keywords></keywords>
    <spline></spline>
    <abilitydescription>
      <p noindent="true">
	The monster is composed of a large number of smaller individuals. Swarms
	suffer maximum damage from area of effect attacks like fire (any damage
	immunity applies). Some swarms are not stopped by doors or windows or
	sometimes even walls. GMs may make a check each round to see if the
	swarm can pass through a barrier,<eg/> wall, window or door. The
	difficulty of the check should depend on the integrity of the barrier
	and the size of the individuals in the swarm.
      </p>
    </abilitydescription>     
  </ability>  
  

  <ability>
    <abilitytitle>Terrifying</abilitytitle>
    <abilityid>terrifying</abilityid>
    <param-rank>3</param-rank>
    <abilitycheck>
      <name>Opposed</name>
      <checktype><fixme/></checktype>
      <poolcost>1</poolcost>
      <apcost><ap4/></apcost>
      <range><ranged-medium/></range>
      <keywords><mettlepool/><npc/><check/></keywords>
      <counter><opponents-mettle-save/></counter>
      <success>No effect</success>
      <fail>Target loses Rank mettle</fail>
      <grimfail>Target loses Rank+1 mettle</grimfail>
      <critfail>Target loses Rank+2 mettle</critfail>
    </abilitycheck>    
    <spline></spline>
    <specializations>
      <specialization>DC11</specialization>
      <specialization>DC13</specialization>
      <specialization>DC15</specialization>
      <specialization>DC17</specialization>
      <specialization>DC19</specialization>
    </specializations>
    <abilitydescription>
      <p noindent="true">
	The creature once revealed in their true form is terrifying.  The
	characters have to make a will check vs rank.  If they fail
	they must lose their turn or flee.
      </p>
    </abilitydescription>
  </ability>  

  
  <ability>
    <abilitytitle>Terrifying Clarion</abilitytitle>
